{"chunk_id": "89700f20ec4b", "text": "This section centers on the public rise of Karna and the beginning of Drona\u2019s long\u2011planned revenge against King Drupada. When Kripa demands Karna declare his royal lineage before fighting Arjuna, Duryodhana immediately crowns him king of Anga so that the duel may proceed. Karna gratefully pledges eternal friendship, sealing the famous alliance between the two men. The moment turns emotional when Karna\u2019s foster father, the charioteer Adhiratha, enters and embraces him; Bhima mocks Karna\u2019s low birth, but Duryodhana fiercely defends him, arguing that valor\u2014not lineage\u2014defines a warrior. Later, Drona demands his pupils capture Drupada as their teacher\u2019s fee. The Kauravas attack first but are routed by Drupada, until the Pandavas\u2014led by Bhima\u2019s brute force and Arjuna\u2019s unmatched archery\u2014enter the battle and begin turning the tide. The chapter highlights themes of social status, loyalty, and the emerging rivalry among the heroes.\nKarna is recognized as a charioteer\u2019s son and mocked, Duryodhana defends him; later Drona sends the princes to capture Drupada, where Arjuna and Bhima dominate the battle.\nThemes: caste and merit, loyalty and friendship, public humiliation, guru dakshina, battlefield prowess", "vector": [0.002389320870861411, -0.016698399558663368, -0.010651269927620888, -0.002934636315330863, -0.007933082059025764, 0.030926939100027084, -0.024430135264992714, -0.0014295656001195312, -0.04236346483230591, -0.02038976550102234, 0.003236657241359353, 0.00879216380417347, 0.011745257303118706, 0.008134429343044758, -0.00039556348929181695, 0.001914476859383285, 0.043732624500989914, -0.01892664283514023, 0.026792610064148903, -0.016094358637928963, -0.014738619327545166, -0.024537520483136177, -0.00856397021561861, 0.030175242573022842, -0.018107831478118896, 0.030202088877558708, 0.00657734414562583, -0.027289265766739845, 0.020913269370794296, -0.028940314427018166,